Venetium 0022 - Windows ARM32 link and platform misc.

BATCH-ARM-1 section 3F, his decision 7 (ARM-1-DECISIONS.md); the three V8 _AddressOfReturnAddress sites live in Venetium 0018. 3 files:
- content/browser/BUILD.gn: dinput8.lib is not linked for current_cpu == "arm" (no ARM32 import lib in SDK 19041; the only lib named by
  the graph that has none). out/arm-rt21's chrome_dll link no longer lists it; x86 unchanged.
- chrome/BUILD.gn: the small initial stack (/STACK:0x80000) for arm as for x86 - Windows ARM32 is a 32-bit build too, and
  chrome_exe_main_win.cc already moves its main thread to a 1.5 MiB fiber under ARCH_CPU_32_BITS (it was 0x800000 = 8 MiB on arm).
- third_party/blink/renderer/platform/wtf/stack_util.cc: GetCurrentStackPosition takes __builtin_frame_address(0) on Windows ARM32
  (clang-cl defines _MSC_VER; _AddressOfReturnAddress is an unresolved external for thumbv7 - TOOLCHAIN-ISSUES B2), and
  GetStackStartImpl gets its missing ARM32 branch (NT_TIB StackBase; it did not compile: non-void function without a return).
Checked (RUNTIME, real arm-rt21 graph after gn gen): stack_util.obj compiles as ARMNT with no _AddressOfReturnAddress reference;
chrome_initial links with /STACK:0x80000; dinput8 gone from chrome_dll's arm libs.

rt2.1-fix v2: the GetCurrentStackPosition hunk is dropped (B2 -> LLVM 0012 + 0020); the GetStackStartImpl ARM32 branch stays.

